the body of kharsa bar is laid to rest  the 23 year old was one of six people  killed in what the u.s. called defensive  precision strikes on Khattab Hezbollah  in southern Iraq but Sabah's family says  he wasn't a fighter but a daily laborer  working at Karbala Airport who had  nothing to do with the iranian-backed  group he worked inside the airport  getting paid $8 per day now that he's  dead  who's gonna think about his kids his  wife his mother where's their guilt  sabado leaves behind a pregnant wife two  children and a family consumed with  grief like many other Iraqis the family  is angry at the US and the Iranian  backed groups for settling scores on  Iraqi soil  Hazara this conflict is between Iran and  America it's none of our business they  should go out and fight it out between  themselves the u.s. strikes followed a  barrage of rockets fired at the Taji  military base north of Baghdad on March  11th killing two American and one  British soldier the Pentagon described  the US response as a success we assess  that each location stored weapons that  would enable lethal operations against  us and coalition forces in Iraq we also  assessed that the destruction of these  sites will degrade Khatib Hizballah's  ability to conduct future strikes but  the American reprisal was followed by a  second rocket attack on target just a  day later raising doubts about the  effectiveness of the US military action  a total of nine people were killed and  dozens wounded in the latest three  tit-for-tat attacks many of the  casualties were members of the Iraqi  security forces who worked with both  sides we don't accept being in the  middle while the two sides to rate their  weapons against each other this has  caused a lot of damage for the Iraqi  army the Iraqi joint operations command  announced both the US and what it  cautiously calls the other side for not  respecting its authority as the highest  military body and for not giving it a  chance to manage the crisis rock for say  there was no chance to finish the  investigation into the first rock  the American side directly reacted with  its strike on Iraqi facilities that  included the army bases and employees  and also the other side started their  attacks which only complicated the  situation but the Iraqi government has  never attributed blame nor has it  published results of investigations for  any of the two dozen rocket attacks that  targeted the coalition over the past six  months the Iraqi government appears  unwilling or unable to stop the groups  responsible for attacks on bases that  house coalition personnel instead it is  called for the implementation of  January's parliamentary decision to  expel all foreign troops from Iraq the  coalition has begun withdrawing soldiers  from smaller bases to consolidate them  in fewer locations and although US  officials say that this move is not  related to the latest rocket attacks it  could pave the way for a partial troop  drawdown over the next few months Simona  14:00 al Jazeera Baghdad
 

